@startuml
title UML sequence - durable event to one economic alert, owned data defect and safe message
participant "Core" as Core
participant "Relay / JetStream" as Relay
participant "Data consumer" as Data
participant "Worker" as Worker
participant "Controls monitoring" as Mon
participant "Data alerts" as Alerts
actor Reviewer
actor Approver
actor Steward
Core -> Relay : journal.batch-posted (outbox)
Relay -> Data : deliver (at least once)
Data -> Data : inbox + aggregate version; duplicate absorbed,\nconflict or gap quarantined
Worker -> Mon : monitoring_tick
Mon -> Mon : each projected fact once per current rule;\nwindow over journal times
alt pattern complete
 Mon -> Mon : anchor = earliest operation in window;\nskip if an overlapping alert exists
 Mon -> Mon : alert + MONITORING case (never customer-visible)
end
Reviewer -> Mon : retrospective scan (bounded)
Mon --> Reviewer : evaluated / created 0 / existing n
Reviewer -> Mon : propose disposition + rationale
Approver -> Mon : approve (different person)
Mon -> Mon : case CLOSED, attributable actions
Worker -> Alerts : quality_scan
Alerts -> Alerts : findings: missing / quarantined / broken / stale /\nundelivered / backlog / aged break / failed message
Alerts -> Alerts : one OPEN alert per (check, subject) + DATA case + next action
Steward -> Alerts : repair_projection(batch)
Alerts -> Data : insert read-model rows only (no balance write)
Worker -> Alerts : next scan clears the alert
Steward -> Alerts : acknowledge cleared alert -> case CLOSED
Worker -> Alerts : derive (dedupe key per economic / document identity)
Worker -> Alerts : deliver: synthetic capture; channel down -> backoff, 6 attempts
@enduml
